Imperaterm 1.0.0
================

The first release. Imperaterm is a lightning fast terminal emulator for
CGTK. Its terminal's logic derives from st.

The terminal
* An xterm to the programs that run in it: TERM is xterm-256color, with
  24 bit colour, the alternate screen, bracketed paste, mouse and focus
  reporting and synchronized output.
* Drawn with OpenGL 3.1, or OpenGL ES 3.0 where there is no such thing
  or IMPERATERM_GLES is set. No GL library is linked, and Help > About
  says which is in use.
* Nothing is drawn when nothing has changed, and what a program writes
  is drawn when it pauses, so that a screen changed in many small
  writes is seen whole. Line drawing and block characters are drawn by
  Imperaterm, so that they join.
* Selections by word, line and block, as the primary selection; the
  clipboard by Ctrl+Shift+C and Ctrl+Shift+V; a scrollback, which the
  wheel scrolls; and larger and smaller text by Ctrl++ and Ctrl+-.

Tabs and windows
* A tab says who is at the terminal and where, user@host: directory,
  as the shell tells it at each prompt by OSC 7 and OSC 1337.
  imperaterm.sh has sh, ash, dash, ksh, bash and zsh tell it, for the
  shell Imperaterm starts and, from profile.d, for login shells; fish
  needs four lines, given in the README. A new tab starts in the
  directory of the one shown.
* Tabs can be renamed, moved along the bar, carried to another window,
  or dropped where there is none to have a window of their own. They
  are at the top of the window or, if chosen, at the bottom.
* All the windows on a display are one Imperaterm, so that a tab can go
  from any to any other and a change in the settings is every window's
  at once. imperaterm --separate is one of its own.
* imperaterm -e runs a command in place of the shell.

Settings
* Edit > Preferences has the font, its size, the colours, the cursor,
  the scrollback, the bell, where the tabs are, the menubar and the
  scrollbar, each in effect as it is made, kept in
  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/imperaterm/imperatermrc.
* Two sets of colours of Imperaterm's own, Default (Dark) and Default
  (Light), whose colours are each read on their ground; well known
  sets by their own names; and Custom, with an editor of its own.

Translations
* Chinese (simplified), French, German, Japanese, Portuguese (Brazil),
  Russian and Spanish, in the program and the desktop file. They were
  machine translated and have not been reviewed by native speakers.

Building
* make check runs the terminal without a window and compares the cells
  and replies with what they should be; tests/bench measures how fast
  it takes text. ./configure --disable-nls builds it in English only.

Not there yet
* Combining characters, colour emoji and ligatures; the kitty keyboard
  and graphics protocols; an input method's preedit text in the
  terminal. The directory of a new tab, and the one a tab shows, are
  found in /proc, so on Linux only.
